From de0555267fb9f3169a21092856da434c064fc137 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:50:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Dashboard figures: refuse cashiers, hide money from stock
 roles

get_dashboard_metrics checked only the warehouse, so any signed-in user,
including a cashier, could ask for the shop's sales, profit, purchases and
expenses. The frontend now sends a cashier straight to the till and hides
these figures, but the browser cannot be the lock.

- require_dashboard_role(): only money roles (the roles that may open
  Reports in the frontend) and stock roles may call it. A cashier, the
  generic "All" and "Guest" roles are refused.
- may_see_money_figures(): money roles get everything; stock roles get
  the stock lists (low stock, pending shipments) with every money figure
  removed.
- Tests added to test_access_control.py (role sets, money visibility,
  stock-only trimming, and the "check comes first" table).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QisqeRhNwdme8fSoc7H2RH
